    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two are support files), and it passes along with the full suite. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` is derived at read time in `OwnerMapper` from the persisted `Owner`. I added the GOLD rule there so it's fully correct with no snapshot staleness, and required no schema or pipeline changes since `householdId` is already stamped onto every household member during create.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (the `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` is generated from this at build time) and updated its description.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Converted the `@Mapper` interface to an abstract class (MapStruct's default component model here is `spring`, so it generates a bean impl that extends it) with an injected `OwnerRepository`. The `membershipTier` mapping now calls a `membershipTier(owner)` method that:\n   - Returns `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same non-blank `householdId`) has **3 or more** members;\n   - Otherwise falls back to the existing SILVER (first with their name + email on file) / BRONZE rules.\n\nThe GET pipeline's `respond` step runs under `readonly-transaction` governance, so the `findAll()` count executes within an active session.\n\n**Verification:** `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` \u2014 which builds a 3-member shared household and asserts the third member is `GOLD` \u2014 passes, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
